  That last row matters: [38;5;153mgreet('world')[39m is the program's [3moutput[0m, not a diagnostic. Routing it through a logger would put
  a timestamp and level on the thing the user came to read, and make it vanish when someone sets [38;5;153mLOG_LEVEL=warn[39m.
  [38;5;153msrc/index.js[39m gets a logger for diagnostics alongside its untouched [38;5;153mconsole.log[39m.

  [1mTesting.[0m The project has no test runner, no linter, no scripts. The redaction walk is the part with real edge cases
  (nesting, arrays, cycles, depth), and it's pure — so it's worth testing, and testable without a browser.

  Two things to decide:
